# Kubernetes triage

## Gate

Load when the user asks about pod/workload health, Pending/CrashLoop, events,
or "what's wrong in the cluster." Skip bare "Kubernetes" with no object or
symptom. Prefer a connected Kubernetes MCP.

## MCP tool map

| Need | Tool |
| --- | --- |
| List namespaces | `namespaces_list` |
| Pods (all ns) | `pods_list` |
| Pods in one ns | `pods_list_in_namespace` |
| One pod | `pods_get` |
| Events | `events_list` (optional `namespace` / `fieldSelector`) |
| Workload / Service / Ingress | `resources_list` / `resources_get` |
| Node CPU/mem | `nodes_top` |
| Node detail | `nodes_stats_summary` |
| Pod CPU/mem | `pods_top` |
| Current kubeconfig context | `configuration_view` (minified; no secrets in reply) |

Never invent namespace, pod, node, or Deployment names — resolve with list/get.

## Procedure

1. Resolve namespace from the user or list namespaces. Do not guess prod.
2. List or get the named workload/pods. Note phase, ready replicas, restarts.
3. Pull Warning events for that object (`fieldSelector` on
   `involvedObject.name` when known).
4. Map symptom → next check (below). Fetch logs only when status/events are
   insufficient — follow `kubernetes-logs`.
5. Report: object, phase/reason, one next action. Keep it short.

## Symptom tree

| Symptom | Likely cause checks |
| --- | --- |
| Pending | Events (FailedScheduling); `nodes_top` / pressure; PVC unbound |
| CrashLoopBackOff | Current + previous logs; exit code; probe failures |
| ImagePullBackOff | Image name/tag; pull secret; registry auth events |
| OOMKilled | `pods_top` / limits; raise memory or fix leak |
| Evicted | Node disk/memory pressure via `nodes_stats_summary` |
| Not Ready | Readiness probe; Service endpoints; `resources_get` on Deployment |

## Defaults

1. Read-only triage is the default. Mutate only under `kubernetes-safety`.
2. Distinguish container state (CrashLoopBackOff) from pod phase (Running).
3. Prefer namespace-scoped lists once the ns is known.
4. OpenShift: `projects_list` only when the cluster exposes projects.
5. Site GitOps paths and overlays stay out of scope — portable object names
   only.
